    "caption": "Black October: the PHP flaw that took government sites offline (Part 1 of 2)\n\nPHP quietly runs around 70% of the websites you use. This month, two critical flaws in it, nicknamed PHP2Shell (severity 9.2/10), leaked a day before the fix was due.\n\nOwn a website? Ask your host which PHP version you're on. Patched: 8.5.12, 8.4.27, 8.3.36, 8.2.35.\n\nPart 2: when hackers hit the real world. Follow so you don't miss it.",
